ethercat (1:1.7.0~rc3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Merge current EtherLab stable-1.7, including FoE output handling,
    external-request device routing, DC synchronization prefill, and Linux
    6.18 and Clang fixes.
  * Fix igc/stmmac builds on Linux 6.12.114 and newer 6.12 stable kernels.
  * Suggest distribution kernel headers instead of recommending them, avoiding
    unwanted kernel image installs for custom-kernel users.
  * Keep EoE configuration symbols available when EoE is disabled, fixing
    builds with LLD 17 and newer.
  * Enable slave identity wildcards in userspace and DKMS configurations.
  * Build source packages as 3.0 (quilt) and fix debug symbol and Clang/dwz
    packaging.
  * Add LLVM-built kernel DKMS CI and the downstream release guide.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:42:27 +0800

ethercat (1:1.7.0~rc2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Align Debian packaging with the 1.6 release line, including the
    ethercat-master package name, udev rules and EoE variants.
  * Require matching master, userspace library and DKMS package versions.
  * Fix DKMS paths for epoch-bearing versions and restore target-side build
    dependencies.
  * Repair EoE DKMS payload, package identity and versioned library provides.
  * Restore Debian 11 and arm64 builds, distro version stamping and automatic
    apt repository ingestion.
  * Add package dependency and DKMS payload checks to release CI.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 10:26:01 +0800

ethercat (1:1.7.0~rc1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First downstream 1.7 release candidate, based on EtherLab stable-1.7.
  * Retain the parallel per-slave scan/configuration and AL recovery work.
  * Include Linux 6.18 and Clang build fixes.
  * Add SII read/write APIs and refresh the SII image after writes, including
    invalidation of the 1.7 SII page cache.
  * Add opt-in ReinitHold so applications can restore volatile slave
    configuration after reconnection before the slave returns to OP.
  * Update the library ABI and document the application restoration workflow.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:45:44 +0800

